Z||000000||Philphine||10-14-2000||08:07 PM||||<BR>did some j-yard searching for a 4th z24 wheel and found a aero nose for my cheap fiero. $100. kinda throws off the plan of making it reliable first but i figured i'd start playing with it before long anyway.<P>i do have a line on a wheel. $125 delivered, but i still hope to find a cheaper one.<P>trying to keep my self from buying the wing i want for a while. about $400. it won't be a cheap thrill any more. <P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe (cheap thrill)||||reg||1
Z||000001||Philphine||10-15-2000||05:43 PM||||call me fickle. after spending yesterday afternoon putting on the aero nose i spent today changing it back. i'm also going to look for the panels that go behind the rear wheels and take rockcrawl's scoops off. won't be getting the f40 wing either (still mean to get it for some future project. i like it too much. the scoops too).<P>i've decided i like the look of it plain for now, plus looking at old posts and seeing a conv. with this body style that looked good. sort of "classic" looking. i'll still do wheels and stereo but i think beyond a gt style wing, lowering, and some kind of front hood vents i'll keep it simple. still hoping to make it a convertible one day.<P>plus i like saying how little i have invested in the car. it's a $300 fiero again.  ||||reg||1
